=>componentDidMount

In function based component,as we know if we want to call api,we can do it in useEffect after first time rendering the component.After getting the data,we can re render the component again.In class based component,we want a same approach that initially render the page first then call the api and then again re render the component.For this , class based component ,provide us a  method of componentDidMount.

So constructor is called first then render is called and then componentDidMount is called.see below example
import React from "react";

class ProfileComponent extends React.Component {
    constructor(props){
        super(props);
        console.log('constructor called');  
    }
    componentDidMount(){
        console.log('component did mount call');       
    }
  render() {
    console.log('render called');
    return (
      <div>
        ProfileComponent 
      </div>
    );
  }
}
export default ProfileComponent;

Result:
constructor called
render called
component did mount call

