Now imp question arrise that why react did not call componentDidMount of first comp and run constructor,render function of second comp?
How this life cycle methods called?

Explanation:
There are 2 phase when react reconsilation process is happening or when react is rendering,this process takes place in 2 process
1-Render Phase                 2-Commit phase
=>Render phase includes your constructor and render method while commit is the phase where react is actually modifying your dom.In this phase,component did mount is called
=>In render phase,your constructor is called and render function is called.
=>In commit phase,component did mount is called

So what happens is render phase appears where react first called constructor method,then render is called.Render method  show the iniial dom screen.After that commit phase appears,component did mount called.This is how life cycle method is worked.See the image of Life cycle method.

=>Which phase is fast? render phase or commit phase ? answer is render phase is fast becasue updating the dom is a difficult task

Now in our example,when there are 2 children (ProfileComponent in about),so  react first tries to patch up the render phases of all the childrens then it will come to commit phase one by one.The reason of this process is that let suppose,if the first children  continues the commit phase ,which means componentDidMount is called and api request is gone.This is the time taken process because api result can be delay and it also delay the render methods of other childrens.Thats why react decided to implement the render phases of all the childrens then move to commit process one by one

